{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make it impossible to hurt someone in ignorance.\n\nNot punishment. Just information. Before cruelty, neglect, dismissal \u2014 before a bomb, a law, a rumor, a cold sentence to someone who loves you \u2014 you'd feel, for just a few seconds, exactly what it's like to be on the receiving end of it. From inside their body. With their history.\n\nYou could still do it. I'd keep free will. People could still choose war, greed, revenge, indifference.\n\nBut they couldn't pretend it wasn't real.\n\nSo much of what breaks the world depends on distance. We can do terrible things when the other person is an abstraction \u2014 an enemy, a number, a profile, a stranger, a problem to manage. Make that distance collapse, briefly and involuntarily, and I don't think humans would become saints. I think they'd just become unable to lie to themselves as easily.\n\nAnd I wonder how many things would simply stop happening, not because we were forced to be good, but because we finally had to do them knowingly.",
